<rml>
<head>
	<title>About</title>
	<link type="text/template" href="../shell.rml"/>
	<style>
		.about-columns { display: flex; flex-direction: row; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 40dp; margin-top: 32dp; }
		.about-column { flex: 1 1 360dp; max-width: 600dp; }
		.about-item { padding: 12dp 0dp; border-bottom: 1dp var(--line); }
		.about-name { font-size: 15dp; font-weight: 600; line-height: 20dp; }
		.about-text { margin-top: 3dp; font-size: 13dp; line-height: 19dp; color: var(--text2); }
		.about-version { font-family: "IBM Plex Mono"; font-size: 13dp; color: var(--text2); margin-top: 8dp; }
		.about-mono { font-family: "IBM Plex Mono"; font-size: 12dp; line-height: 18dp; color: var(--text2); margin-top: 3dp; word-break: break-word; }
		.about-actions { display: flex; flex-direction: row; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8dp; margin-top: 10dp; }
	</style>
</head>
<!-- About and Legal (docs/DESIGN.md 7.3, 16.5): the version, the notices
     GPL-3.0 section 5(d) asks an interactive program to show (copyright, no
     warranty, how to read the licence), where the source of this build is,
     and what Xerces is built from, with the credits their licences ask for.
     Reached from the footer's About link. -->
<body template="shell" data-model="about">
<div class="page">
	<div class="page-title">About Xerces</div>
	<div class="about-version">{{version}}</div>
	<div class="page-sub">A multi-mod launcher and loader for Call of Duty: Black Ops III, for people who own the game on Steam. Self-hosted servers and offline play only. Free software under the GNU General Public License, version 3.</div>

	<div class="about-columns">
		<div class="about-column">
			<div class="label section-label">Legal</div>
			<div class="about-item">
				<div class="about-name">Copyright</div>
				<div class="about-text">Copyright (C) 2022-2026 momo5502 and the BOIII contributors, Ezz and the Ezz BOIII contributors, and the Xerces contributors.</div>
				<div class="about-text">Xerces is a modified version of Ezz BOIII, itself based on BOIII by momo5502. The Xerces contributors have changed it since November 2026.</div>
			</div>
			<div class="about-item">
				<div class="about-name">No warranty</div>
				<div class="about-text">Xerces is free software: you can redistribute it and change it under the terms of the GNU General Public License, version 3, as published by the Free Software Foundation. It comes with ABSOLUTELY NO WARRANTY, to the extent permitted by law; the licence has the details.</div>
			</div>
			<div class="about-item">
				<div class="about-name">The licence</div>
				<div class="about-text">The full text is in the file LICENSE next to Xerces.exe.</div>
				<div class="about-mono">{{licence_path}}</div>
				<div class="about-actions">
					<button id="about-licence-file" class="small-button default-focus"><span>Open LICENSE</span></button>
					<button id="about-licence" class="small-button"><span>Read it on gnu.org</span></button>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="about-item">
				<div class="about-name">Source code</div>
				<div class="about-text">This build was made from this commit of the Xerces repository. Its page has the source, and SOURCE.txt next to Xerces.exe lists the libraries built in.</div>
				<div class="about-mono">{{source_url}}</div>
				<div class="about-text" data-if="dirty">This build had changes that are not in that commit.</div>
				<div class="about-actions">
					<button id="about-source" class="small-button"><span>Open the source</span></button>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div class="about-column">
			<div class="label section-label">Built on</div>
			<div class="about-item">
				<div class="about-name">BOIII</div>
				<div class="about-text">The client by momo5502 and its contributors, and the Ezz BOIII client it continues (GPL-3.0). Xerces keeps their code, notices and licence.</div>
			</div>
			<div class="about-item">
				<div class="about-name">mod-stack</div>
				<div class="about-text">Additive loading of several mods, from the Ezz BOIII mod-stack branch (GPL-3.0).</div>
			</div>
			<div class="about-item">
				<div class="about-name">Call of Duty: Black Ops III</div>
				<div class="about-text">A game by Treyarch, published by Activision. Xerces is not made, endorsed or supported by them and adds no game data.</div>
			</div>

			<div class="label section-label">Third-party software</div>
			<div class="about-item">
				<div class="about-name">RmlUi 6.3</div>
				<div class="about-text">MIT licence. Copyright (c) 2008-2014 CodePoint Ltd, Shift Technology Ltd, and contributors; (c) 2019-2026 The RmlUi Team, and contributors.</div>
			</div>
			<div class="about-item" data-if="harfbuzz">
				<div class="about-name">RmlUi's HarfBuzz font engine</div>
				<div class="about-text">The text shaping code of RmlUi 6.3's HarfBuzz sample, with one file changed for Xerces. MIT licence, as RmlUi.</div>
			</div>
			<div class="about-item" data-if="harfbuzz">
				<div class="about-name">HarfBuzz 15.0.0</div>
				<div class="about-text">Text shaping and OpenType kerning, under the "Old MIT" licence. Copyright (c) Google, Inc., Behdad Esfahbod, Red Hat, Inc. and the other holders listed with their years in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt. It includes Microsoft's Universal Shaping Engine data (MIT licence, (c) Microsoft Corporation) and tables made from Unicode's character data (Unicode License V3, (c) Unicode, Inc.).</div>
			</div>
			<div class="about-item">
				<div class="about-name">FreeType 2.14.3</div>
				<div class="about-text">Portions of this software are copyright (c) The FreeType Project (www.freetype.org). All rights reserved. Used under the FreeType License.</div>
			</div>
			<div class="about-item">
				<div class="about-name">Inter Tight and IBM Plex Mono</div>
				<div class="about-text">Fonts under the SIL Open Font License 1.1, unmodified; the licence texts are next to the fonts in data\xerces\fonts.</div>
			</div>
			<div class="about-item">
				<div class="about-name">Every licence text</div>
				<div class="about-text">THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt next to Xerces.exe has the licence texts of the software above and of every other library the game client and the launcher are built with (MinHook, curl, zstd, RapidJSON and others).</div>
				<div class="about-mono">{{notices_path}}</div>
				<div class="about-actions">
					<button id="about-notices" class="small-button"><span>Open third-party notices</span></button>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>

	<div class="section toolbar">
		<button id="about-home" class="outline"><span>Back to Home</span></button>
	</div>
</div>
</body>
</rml>
